& [ImplementationProofChecklist: IR5SurfaceProjectionPrototype] is the proof checklist for later implementation activation
  + [proof_check] is implementation files match ImplementationFileInventory: IR5SurfaceProjectionPrototype
  + [proof_check] is external dependency set remains empty unless a dependency-authorizing activation slice accepts a package
  + [proof_check] is authority display envelope rejects missing authority notice, missing source refs, missing route, hidden stop-state, and lower-tier authority promotion
  + [proof_check] is projection state envelope prevents ready display when blocked, stale, faulted, interrupted, contested, pending-review, unsupported, or refused evidence exists
  + [proof_check] is action route classifier emits request, refusal, or SOP-first interrupt records without mutating source authority
  + [proof_check] is manager, worker, narrative, debug, conversation, adapter, Langflow, runtime handoff, and operation projections satisfy fixture plan cases
  + [proof_check] is runtime checkpoints, generated traces, generated reports, dry-runs, human approvals, carrier state, and Langflow diagrams remain non-authoritative
  + [proof_check] is generated projection and report writers refuse paths outside accepted generated roots
  + [proof_check] is fixture runner reads only tracked fixture source and expected ledgers and writes only generated outputs
  + [proof_check] is source files, expected ledgers, and tracked SOP authority are not mutated by projection code or tests
  + [proof_check] is operations simulator implementation, operations control, and live machine control remain absent

  = must: require completion review before any implementation output is accepted
  = must: fail implementation review if any proof check fails

